{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{1,3} |D559|D560|D451|gate 1|gate 4'\"' clean-arch/PRD.md docs/CURRENT_STATE.md docs/DECISIONS.md docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md\"","aggregated_output":"docs/CURRENT_STATE.md:1:# Current state\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:103:## Future evidence scoring (D372)\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:107:## Latest decision (D369)\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:128:## What runs\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:140:## Open defects\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:159:## One next task\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:281:**The core-problem council (D559, 2026-11-15; asked by Alex after the week's result, his words in the decision log), all at $0:** the product\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:294:**The reflection council (D560, 2026-11-15, asked by Alex; his words in the decision log), all at $0:** the goal is a\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:302:then D559's comparison. The role of the six answer-choice lines is put to him after the pilot. No gate, line or frozen piece\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:311:- **The two-week product-condition run (D563, D564):** read in five ways; gate 1 (Alex's six lines) is not met there either (7 or\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:323:- **Waiting on Alex (D560, unchanged):** his half hour on the pilot's cards\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:325:  `~/.hivemind-keys/pilot-deck-1/`), then the six lines' role, then D559's wider question.\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:427:loop resumes on Alex's rulings (his page, `DECISION-PAGE-2026-11-16.md`: Deck 1, the six lines' role, D559, D520, D571, live\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:627:  citing D439. Paid spending in this period: $0.83 (gate 1) of a $40 ceiling (Claude's setting); gate 2 sent on Alex's word (D438).\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:656:- **The full run (D451) completed** (`poc/data/clean-e2e-full-2026-11-13/`, 05:44–08:33; c2's Step 1 redone after a dropped response,\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:1:# The lean path toward production: round log (Alex, 2026-11-14: \"小步快跑\")\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:3:## 0. Frame\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:22:## 1. Step 1: statements dated after their article ($0) — the premise does not hold; nothing is built\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:38:## 2. Step 2: one fresh week, one draw a system — frozen before any send\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:99:## 3. Step 2's result and step 3 (D489): not clear; no system chosen; one product choice goes to Alex\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:120:## 4. Step 3: Alex opens the test of revenue and margin questions on the new system (D490)\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:164:## 5. Reflection council mx (D492, D493): what the traces say, and the next step\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:201:## 6. Alex opens the new version of the record: a source and a fixed-form period on each figure (D495)\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:230:## 7. The figure fields, second version (D497): empty unless the article says it\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:262:## 8. The record test on unread articles (D499): c8's record against c22's\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:290:## 9. A financial table built by code from what the adopted request keeps (D501): a $0 reader test\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:319:## 10. The table on the fresh week (D503): can a reader find the figures of the three matters the new system had no question for? $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:344:## 11. Do the kept financial figures reach the judgements of related questions? (D505) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:366:## 12. How large is the gap? A census over everything the new system kept in the fresh week (D507) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:388:## 13. Does one missing fact change one stored judgement? Six calls (D510, D511; under D439 after Alex went inactive, D509)\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:405:## 14. Reflection council \"my\" (D512, under D439): step back from the corner; a decision page for Alex\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:442:## 15. Could an affordable comparison choose between the systems? The sizing (D516, D517; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:458:## 16. The same week, both systems, side by side (D517, D518; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:475:## 17. When does the judge give an answer its evidence does not support? Census and four accounts (D518, D519; under D439) $0.0041\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:499:## 18. The judge line stops at a choice for Alex; the old system's duplicate questions traced (D520; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:518:## 19. The same-day candidates against the decision in force (D521; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:534:## 20. A probe designed twice on a wrong premise, withdrawn; the duplicates traced to the comparison step (D522, D523; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:550:## 21. The $0 proof of D375's per-article list: design reviewed three times, stages 1 and 2 built (D524 to D526; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:566:## 22. The D375 proof: stages 3 and 4 run; not yet passed (D527; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:581:## 23. The D375 proof: every registered check built and holding (D527; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:593:## 24. The D375 proof passes as a bounded serial proof; the measurement is to be designed small (D528; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:606:## 25. Eligible cases for measuring D375, read on the stored week (D528; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:618:## 26. The trace into the final requests finds one question that never received its guidance (D529; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:633:## 27. The missing-input case is recorded; its mechanism is sized before any test (D530; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:643:## 28. A missing figure explains three of the ten settled unsupported answers (D530; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:654:## 29. The two filings traced: each a written rule working as written (D531; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:667:## 30. No common mechanism from two cases; the dependency lead goes under D368 (D532; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:677:## 31. The dependency lead stops: the facts would have to travel the other way (D532; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:687:## 32. This stretch closed and consolidated; the next slice is D368's channel on its own terms (D533; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:697:## 33. D368's dependency channel on stored, correctly directed cases (D533; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:707:## 34. The channel assessment corrected: its lines came from the future (D534; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:717:## 35. The stored chronology: no supporting conclusion exists that had not read its receiver (D534, part 1; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:724:## 36. D368's ordering and propagation exercised with fake outputs (D534, part 2; under D439) $0\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md:735:## 37. The ordering proof accepted as a wiring result; two $0 checks before a measurement design (D535; under D439)\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEA