el built the way a hedge-fund analyst works\nclean-arch/PRD.md:14:## 1. Vision, problems and what is done differently\nclean-arch/PRD.md:16:### 1.1 The vision: a market world model\nclean-arch/PRD.md:55:### 1.2 The problems it answers\nclean-arch/PRD.md:79:### 1.3 Why the running pipeline was rebuilt\nclean-arch/PRD.md:102:### 1.4 What the new system does differently\nclean-arch/PRD.md:120:beforehand (D489). The weakest point is named (D559): the system often cannot turn an important matter into a question it can answer\nclean-arch/PRD.md:126:### 1.5 The gates before it replaces the running pipeline\nclean-arch/PRD.md:139:## 2. Architecture at a glance\nclean-arch/PRD.md:190:## 3. The information the system works with\nclean-arch/PRD.md:207:## 4. Step 1: read the item\nclean-arch/PRD.md:209:### Input\nclean-arch/PRD.md:216:### What the model decides\nclean-arch/PRD.md:241:### Output\nclean-arch/PRD.md:250:### Example\nclean-arch/PRD.md:262:## 5. Step 2: find and compare related evidence\nclean-arch/PRD.md:264:### Why this is separate\nclean-arch/PRD.md:268:### Find candidate evidence\nclean-arch/PRD.md:276:### Compare with Jev\nclean-arch/PRD.md:317:## 6. Step 3: save evidence and links\nclean-arch/PRD.md:331:## 7. Step 4: judge the thesis\nclean-arch/PRD.md:338:### Two parts\nclean-arch/PRD.md:347:### What the ladder step decides\nclean-arch/PRD.md:364:### Where it stands\nclean-arch/PRD.md:377:## 8. How the system is measured, and where it stands\nclean-arch/PRD.md:379:### The measuring stick\nclean-arch/PRD.md:388:- **Use on unseen news** (gate 4, D484): readers first list the big matters in a week of news, then check what each system covered,\nclean-arch/PRD.md:391:### Where each step stands\nclean-arch/PRD.md:397:| Step 4a (gate 1) | Alex's six lines (D400). | Not met in nine readings. | Section 7 |\nclean-arch/PRD.md:399:| End to end (gate 3) | D427, D431. | Owed. Diagnostics so far: seeded 18, 18, 17 against 17, 15, 16 of 23, inconclusive (D392–D394); same-day July census 2, 1, 0 against 1, 1, 1 settled agreements, every loss at opening (D451). | [Comparison](e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/) |\nclean-arch/PRD.md:400:| Use on unseen news (gate 4) | Proposed, not Alex's. | One fresh week, one draw: big matters covered 2 of 5 against 4 of 5; last answers supported 6 of 7 against 10 of 15; \"not clear\" (D489). | [Week result](../docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md) |\nclean-arch/PRD.md:402:### What the measurements say\nclean-arch/PRD.md:406:  grades (D395, D451). Where it was given the facts, the judge reasoned as the expert readers did (section 1.2). The judge's own test\nclean-arch/PRD.md:408:- **The core problem is forming answerable questions** (D559): a worthwhile matter is left without an answerable question, or a\nclean-arch/PRD.md:418:## 9. Walk one item through the system\nclean-arch/PRD.md:440:## 10. Open questions\nclean-arch/PRD.md:442:1. **Forming answerable questions** (gate 1; D559). How the system turns more worthwhile matters into questions it can answer, without\nclean-arch/PRD.md:463:## 11. Design boundary\nclean-arch/PRD.md:471:## 12. Step 1 prompt: c8, adopted (D387)\nclean-arch/PRD.md:501:### What the model receives\nclean-arch/PRD.md:507:### System prompt\nclean-arch/PRD.md:685:### Closing check\nclean-arch/PRD.md:708:### Proposed per-item input\nclean-arch/PRD.md:735:### Structured-output schema\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1026:### Illustrative output for the sample input (earlier Luna draft, kept as history)\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1095:### Mapping to the Step 1 diagram\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1107:### Request review and remaining limits\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1115:## 13. Step 2 prompt: Jev request (frozen)\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1119:### What Jev receives\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1127:### The question\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1140:### How the answers become the outcome\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1147:### The later link when a thesis opens\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1159:## 14. Existing components to reference during the rebuild\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1163:### Thesis and evidence database\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1171:### Source pool and golden validation data\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1182:### Source data standing in for Hummingbird\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1190:### Existing extraction reference split\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1203:### Diagram-to-code map\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1218:## 15. Future design: entity relationships and cross-entity linkage\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1222:### Why this is needed\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1226:### Separate, asynchronous relationship maintenance\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1236:### Illustration: a supplier disruption\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1240:### Questions to resolve before cross-entity production use\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1252:## 16. Earlier record\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1:# Decisions\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:23:## Open for Alex\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:30:## Settled in this consolidation\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:49:## 1. System (PRD 00)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:75:## Latest decision: remove the separate earnings-report import (D370)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:79:## Latest decision: current and future financial evidence (D371)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:83:## Latest decision: continue scoring on the existing gold (D373)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:87:## Latest decision: read the current library for each item (D375)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:91:## Latest decision: return complete evidence without the 1 MB rejection (D376)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:95:## Latest decision: return the full question catalog without the 150 KB rejection (D377)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:99:## 2. Research universe (PRD 01)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:110:## 3. Classification (PRD 02)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:120:## 4. Config (PRD 03)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:129:## 5. Dispatch (PRD 04)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:137:## 6. Extraction (PRD 05 and the extraction standard)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:172:## 7. Thesis library (PRD 06)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:239:## 8. Closing and pull mode (PRD 07, PRD 08)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:251:## 9. Review pool (PRD 09)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:257:## 10. Current phase: filing that links facts the way an analyst does (PRD 10)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:294:## 12. Idea API and service (docs/poc/idea-card.md, docs/poc/service.md)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:312:## 13. Data (README, \"Local requirements and data\")\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:320:## 14. Operations (README, AGENTS §9)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:332:## 15. Working rules (AGENTS.md)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:340:## Index\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:795:| D451 | 2026-11-13 | Launch the full run: clean c1–c3 (ladder three passes) and production p1–p3 for 2026-07-01..07-14, same day, ledger $14.84; readings committed before the send (council consensus, D439) | in force | `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/READING-COMMITMENT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:902:| D558 | 2026-11-15 | Under D439 (council consensus): the audit of the event-reference and unlisted-part classes finds no bounded, product-relevant repair ready; D400's lines unchanged, the first gate recorded as not met; put to Alex: that record and one request, to finish the unfinished week as a diagnostic (matching and judge, pipeline ledger at most $0.80) after a $0 proof of the continuation; nothing sent without his word | in force; its proposed next task superseded by D559 | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/second-week/PROMPT-AUDIT-TWO-CLASSES.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:903:| D559 | 2026-11-15 | Core-problem council (Alex's request; council consensus): the product problem is forming answerable questions, no single cause proven; the clean measurements examined start from empty, against the start-state record of 2026-11-05 (now numbered here; a contemporaneous account, to be confirmed by Alex); the empty-start results and the gate record stay; to Alex: confirm the return to a real starting library and, on his word, one small same-article comparison (carried library against empty) after five $0 proofs | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-3/cold-codex-5.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:904:| D560 | 2026-11-15 | Reflection council (Alex's request; council consensus): the goal is a continuing research library whose answers show their reasons, with no single number for \"ready\"; the measuring method is a major part of the impasse beside real product defects, not apportioned; next a $0 pilot of Alex's own product-level review on the stored fresh week (16 cards, 3 repeats, controls, three completeness sheets), then D559's comparison; the role of the six answer-choice lines put to him after the pilot; nothing changes or is sent | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-4/council-codex-3.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:905:| D561 | 2026-11-16 | Alex: \"go\": D559's small comparison is sent as designed (11 opening articles of the week of 10-06, each read from the week of 09-22's library and from empty, 22 reads, ledger ceiling $1.00); read as fixed in its design; his Deck 1 marks still wait; D559's wider confirmation asked again with the result | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-library/DESIGN.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:906:| D562 | 2026-11-16 | The small comparison (council consensus): with last week's library the first step re-opened none of the 4 held questions (16 questions opened from empty against 4, none duplicating the library; 17 of 27 homes right and 2 wrong by both readers); it did not open the equity-commitments question the empty read opened and lost a DOJ/FTC question; between the rule's two outcomes, reported as it is; nothing about final answers; next to Alex: Deck 1, then D559's wider question, then the six lines | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-library/RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:908:| D564 | 2026-11-16 | The fortnight read (council consensus): no held question re-opened; gate 1 still not met in the product condition (7 or 5 of 13 right); no last answer unsupported by both readers, 6 of 12 contested; the page fix (processing steps and completed days at the writer) accepted for completed replays; the due-date class is one matter; next a $0 sizing of D505's company-figure delivery gap, facts linked elsewhere included | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-run/RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:911:| D567 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (council rounds 25 and 26): the new system's daily loop closes due questions with production's closing step, walks calendar days and owns its store sequence; accepted on tests, mutants, the unchanged extension proof and a replay to 2027-04-02; next a $0 check of gate 1's reading method on independently established sound answer choices | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-run/CLOSING-DESIGN.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:912:| D568 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (council rounds 27 to 31): gate 1's reading of the fortnight repeated from the start by the unchanged tooling (identical packets, fresh readers and third readers of both families) and compared send by send by the gate's own accounting; it reports agreement and difference only; the lines unchanged | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/gate1-stick/DESIGN.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:913:| D569 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (council round 32): gate 1's verdict reproduced by its method on the fortnight (not a validity proof); D397's 'shown beside the answer as not judged' is missing from the product's page; next a $0 design and proof of that display path, judgements unchanged | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/gate1-stick/RESULT.md` |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
