{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"ls poc/data/clean-lean-week-2026-11-14/week-r2/c1; ls poc/data/clean-lean-week-2026-11-14/week/p1; rg -n '279|145|109|D382|revenue|gross margin' docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md\"","aggregated_output":"cases\ncases.log\njudge\njudge-inputs.json\njudge.log\nladder\nladder.log\nlaunch.lock\npreconditions.log\nrun.json\nstep1\nstep1.log\nstep2\nstep2.log\nlaunch.lock\npreconditions.log\nprod\nprod.log\nrun.json\n6:three matters the clean path lacks are the company's own revenue and margin, which its request forbids as questions (D382). The second rests\n8:both families call only one judgement unsupported, production's data-center revenue.\n24:| links to questions | 196 | 449 (126 on FY2027 total revenue, 94 on data-center revenue) |\n31:| M01 FY2027 revenue (total or data center) | both | **missed** | opened (v2, v4) |\n32:| M02 FY2028 revenue | both | **missed** | opened (v3, v5) |\n33:| M03 FY2028 gross margin against the 72%–73% outlook | both | **missed** | opened (v10) |\n34:| M04 supply and capacity purchase commitments ($279B at Q2) | both | opened (clean-2) | **missed** |\n36:| M06 FY2027 gross margin | one | missed | missed |\n37:| M07 Vera Rubin revenue shipments in Q3 | one | opened (Claude) / a later deadline that does not settle Q3 (Codex) | the same split |\n38:| M08 AMD's 2027 data-center revenue | one | missed | missed |\n48:| duplicate of another of its own | 0 | 3 by both: FY2028 growth of FY2028 revenue, Rubin by end-2027 of Rubin by January 2027, the second RTX Pro 5500 question; Claude adds data-center revenue of total revenue |\n51:- Production has no supply-commitments question: its one kept statement on the $279 billion is linked to the credit-support question (v1).\n54:  any period, on its own\", opens nothing and keeps the statements; 109 of 235 steps' reasoning names that sentence. The request sends such\n55:  figures to \"an open thesis about its revenue or earnings path\", which nothing in an empty library is: 145 kept statements of the company's\n70:Supported by both families: **clean 6 of 7 (86%), production 10 of 15 (67%)**. Unsupported by both: one, production's data-center revenue (v4):\n83:What weakens each half: A's three-matter gap is one sentence of the clean request, a product rule (D382), not a capability. B compares 7\n91:How each system treats the company's own revenue and margin: three of the five matters, 145 kept statements no judgement reads on one side;\n96:Claude's first candidate for a next step was a narrow door on the clean path: open a revenue or margin question only when the item holds both\n102:| M01 FY2027 revenue | 7 | **0** | the consensus alone ($406 billion, $412 billion, \"about 90% growth\"), or the company's guide for one quarter ($108 billion); the company gives no outlook for the year |\n103:| M02 FY2028 revenue | 8 | 2 with figures (70% guided \"against the 45% the Street had modelled\", a gap already closed: the consensus is now about $672 billion), 1 in words | the 70% outlook alone (5 articles) |\n104:| M03 FY2028 gross margin | 2 | 1 (the 72%–73% outlook, \"analysts assume margins hold roughly steady\", memory prices above what management expected) | the outlook alone |\n106:- **The pair does not cover the gap** (it never opens FY2027 revenue): the candidate is dropped, as its falsifier said.\n107:- **Why the readers listed these matters:** every one of their 24 revenue and margin entries gives the reason \"main driver\" (the company's\n110:- **A counter-example on production's side:** its data-center revenue question (v4) was opened from an article that holds only last\n111:  quarter's reported figure (\"$89 billion of data-center revenue out of $96.2 billion\"), no outlook and no expectation. It is the question\n112:  one family calls a duplicate of total revenue, and its judgement is the one both families call unsupported.\n114:  (D382, D384). The week shows what each answer costs; it does not show a narrower rule that would get both.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
