{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/main-numbers/RESULT.md'","aggregated_output":"# Revenue and margin questions on the new system: the probe's step one — result (D490), 2026-11-14\n\n**Answer: step one fails by the lines written before the send, on one of them.** The test arm (c20) opens the revenue and margin\nquestions and files their figures, with no question on other statement lines, quarters or other companies' figures. But on the one case\nwhere it could be judged, it does not open the Vera Rubin question: 0 of 3 sends against the adopted request's 2 of 3, and all three sends\nfile \"Vera Rubin has entered full production\" under the new revenue question. Why is not settled: the stored reasoning gives two reasons\nside by side, the article's missing shipment date (which also stopped the adopted request in its one send that did not open it) and the\nrevenue question as a ready home. The line stops here and goes to Alex; step two and the fresh week are not run.\n\nMaterial: ten stored states of the fresh week, the adopted request (c8) and the arm (c20), three sends each, 60 sends, all valid; $1.02\n(ceiling $2.00). Read by Claude send by send (`answers-listing-stage1.txt`) and by two blind reader families who did not know the arms\n(`codex-reader.jsonl`, `claude-reader.jsonl`; `tally-stage1.txt`). One draw of three sends a case: the counts show mechanisms on these\ncases, not rates.\n\n## The lines\n\n| line | result | detail |\n|---|---|---|\n| Opened: fiscal 2027 revenue | met | 9 of 9 sends on its three cases, both families; always total revenue, as a level |\n| Opened: fiscal 2028 gross margin | met | 6 of 6 sends on its two cases, both families |\n| Opened: fiscal 2028 revenue | **disputed between the readers** | a question in 13 of 15 sends. Six count for both families (two cases: levels, and one growth rate that names the year it grows over). The other seven ask a growth rate with no base year named (\"What total revenue growth will NVIDIA report for fiscal 2028?\"), which the rule counts only when the base year is named: Codex counts none of them, Claude five. By Codex 2 of 5 cases, by Claude 3 of 5; three were needed |\n| Kept and linked | met | all ten named facts kept in every send of both arms; where the arm opened the fact's question, the fact was linked to it (both families), except under the disputed growth questions |\n| Number card | none | 0 of 30 sends, both families: no question on EPS, net income, a quarter, a later year or another company |\n| Twice in one answer | none | 0 of 30 sends, both families |\n| Suppression, supply commitments (k1) | control absent | c8 opened it in 1 of 3 sends, c20 in 2 of 3: cannot be judged |\n| **Suppression, Vera Rubin (k2)** | **fails** | c8 2 of 3 (and in the stored draw); **c20 0 of 3** |\n| Reported: a bare reported figure (g1) | no question | 0 of 3 in both arms |\n\nThe disputed line does not change the verdict: step one fails on suppression either way.\n\n## What the answers show beyond the lines\n\n- **The Vera Rubin question: two possible causes, not separated (council round 16).** In c20's sends the reasoning weighs the product\n  question and gives the missing shipment date as the reason not to open it (\"We don't open due to no date\"; \"no separate thesis because\n  the event has already occurred and no date for shipments\"), and it files the statement under the new revenue question (\"If we don't\n  create, link to revenue\"; \"Link Vera Rubin to new revenue thesis? It informs future revenue path … yes\"). The adopted request's one send\n  that did not open it gives the same date reason (\"no product_node thesis possible without a date\"); its other two set the fiscal\n  year-end as the check date and opened it. Three sends an arm cannot tell whether the revenue question made \"do not open\" easier or the\n  arms simply fell on different sides of the same doubt. Where the Vera Rubin question is already open (later articles), c20 links such\n  statements to it as c8 does, sometimes to the revenue question as well.\n- **The revenue question takes in more than the company's figures.** Of the 97 statements c20 linked to a new revenue or margin question, 66\n  carry a company figure and 31 do not: the supply bottleneck, Vera Rubin production, and, on one article, five statements about AMD in two\n  of three sends, filed as \"competitive evidence\" under NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 revenue (c8 leaves them without a question). This is the\n  pattern of production's revenue question, which held 126 statements in the fresh week.\n- **Statements with a question.** Over the same 30 sends, statements with no question fall from 118 (c8) to 45 (c20).\n- **Shape follows the article.** A level where the article states a level (the consensus in dollars), mostly a growth rate where it states\n  the 70% outlook: over a week this can give one fiscal year two shapes, which step two was written to test and did not run.\n- **Not asked for, in scope:** the fiscal 2027 gross margin, opened on three articles (in 6 of 9 sends there).\n- **Supply commitments** opened by c8 in only 1 of 3 sends on the article where the stored draw opened it: the adopted request's own spread.\n\n## What it means\n\n- The hypothesis held on what it predicted (the questions open once the rule allows them, without number cards) and met a stop condition\n  written beforehand: on the one judged case a product question was not opened. The line stops by that condition; the cause is a lead.\n- The new questions do change where news goes: product and competitor statements are filed under revenue. Whether each such link is right\n  is a question of filing quality the probe did not judge (the standard lets product, demand and competitor news inform a revenue question\n  when it bears on it); it is the pattern D382 was wary of, not a proof of it.\n- Not shown: that a revenue question must swallow a product question; that statements without a company figure should never be linked to\n  revenue; that either system is better; that the kept figures are usable today.\n- **Where the kept figures stand today (counted at $0 on the week's clean draw):** 567 statements reach the judge's store and 382 of them\n  have no question; the 70% outlook and the $406 billion and $412 billion estimates appear in none of the 37 judgement requests; when a\n  question opened, the later-linking step judged 516 earlier statements and linked 2. The use Alex approved on 2026-11-08 for a kept figure\n  (\"it becomes evidence when a related view opens and the reference when views are judged\", `LOG.md` §17) is not happening for them.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D505|D608|D606|D607|D592|D603' docs/DECISIONS.md\"","aggregated_output":"849:| D505 | 2026-11-15 | Alex: the kept financial figures should reach the judgements of related questions (not a table, not questions of their own; D382 and D384 stand); first a $0 check on the stored fresh-week run: is a kept financial figure a judgement should have received absent from its request | in force; the check ran (D506) | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md` §11 |\n908:| D564 | 2026-11-16 | The fortnight read (council consensus): no held question re-opened; gate 1 still not met in the product condition (7 or 5 of 13 right); no last answer unsupported by both readers, 6 of 12 contested; the page fix (processing steps and completed days at the writer) accepted for completed replays; the due-date class is one matter; next a $0 sizing of D505's company-figure delivery gap, facts linked elsewhere included | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-run/RESULT.md` |\n936:| D592 | 2026-11-16 | Stage B's control line: an unchanged re-send stays at 4 of 8, delivery of three facts reaches at most 7, the eighth needs an unproven two-step change; the 7-control course is not started for the line's sake; the live-service operating contract resumed as a $0 design (D575's rows, a falsifier), back to the council before any build | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md` |\n947:| D603 | 2026-11-16 | Slice 5 built and proven at $0: `service.open_pinned` (one pinned opener for the API and MCP, `StoreUnreadable` naming the path on an opening, `BEGIN` or pinning failure) and an explicit 5 s reader busy timeout; proofs 5a, 5b, 6a, 6b (stand-in), 7′ (88 outcomes against an independent pre-partial-day reference) and 8′; 346 + 192 tests, 6 of 6 mutants | in force | `live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md` (Slice 5) |\n950:| D606 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (council round 148), reversibly: next product test from a real earlier library (empty starts as diagnostics); Alex's six lines and accounting stay in force; postponement provisionally reads Still open (reversed by D607); D520/D571 running behaviour retained; P1 not taken; next a $0 audit of the postponed-event class (by topic and matter, full rungs, guards) | in force | `reflection-4/council-codex-148.md` |\n951:| D607 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (council round 149): D606's postponement reading reversed provisionally (a formal decision that a dated event will not happen by its due day rules it out; authorities by D420; forecast-versus-decision guard kept); the postponement repair route closes (no missing general rule; Taiwan p3 isolated); next a $0 audit of the shared fiscal-year note's consumers and effects | in force | `unlisted-parts/fresh-a2/postponement/AUDIT-RESULT.md` |\n952:| D608 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (council round 150): the fiscal-note lead closes as cleanup-only (no demonstrated product effect; the clause is not inert because check 5 refuses a pre-year-end day; the reader split's cause not established); a reflection council (fresh Codex, cold read) follows | in force | `unlisted-parts/fresh-a2/fiscal-note/RESULT.md` |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-run/RESULT.md'","aggregated_output":"# The product condition, end to end over two weeks with the library kept: the reading (D563), 2026-11-16\n\n**Answer: in this one draw, with the library of week 1 held, the six questions week 2 opened duplicated none it held (both\nfamilies), and the step that writes answer choices wrote them for 12 of 13 topics in all three attempts, but the choices do not meet Alex's six lines (gate 1: 7 or 5 of 13\ntopics right against a scaled 11). Of the 12 last answers, none is unsupported by both families and 6 are contested\nby at least one of three readers, for several different reasons. The company's own numbers have no home by product rule, and\nneither reader family predicted that any not delivered would change one of the 12 answers; two statements over-read their\npassages; the product's page could not show the new system's library (fixed at the writer, D564). One draw, one company,\none fortnight; week 2's later steps were regenerated with week 1's, not a live two-week history.**\n\nRun: `poc/data/clean-carried-run-2026-11-16/` (week 1 the stored run of 2026-09-22..28 from empty; week 2 2026-09-29..10-05, 241\nnever-sent articles, read from week 1's library; the later steps regenerated over the fortnight; ledger $3.476 of $6.00, no\nrefusal). Plan frozen before any answer was read (`PLAN.md`, sha256 in `PLAN.sha256`); my own read stored first (`OWN-READ.md`).\n\n## What the run did\n\n| | Week 1 (from empty) | Week 2 (library kept) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Articles | 235 | 241 |\n| Topics opened | 7 | 6 |\n| Kept statements with no link | 389 of 569 (68%) | 339 of 626 (54%) |\n\nAnswer choices over the fortnight: **12 of 13 topics written in all three attempts**; the one declined in all three is\n\"venture funding for physical AI companies\" (no listed theme covers it; the two opening readers split on its worth, my own read says not worth holding). Written is not right: read against\nAlex's six lines (reading A below), they do not meet them. For comparison, from an empty start: the week of 10-06, 4 of 13\ntopics declined at least once, 2 every time, and agreed faults beyond refusals; July, 21 of 104 declined in two or three attempts.\nDifferent weeks and articles: an observation, not a measured difference.\n\n## Reading A: Alex's six lines on the fortnight's answer choices (`poc/data/clean-carried-run-2026-11-16/stage-a/report.txt`)\n\nThe October tooling unchanged: two families apart (39 valid rows each), 24 sends disputed, a third reader of each family on 34\npoints; every unresolved point counted both ways. **Gate 1 is not met:** line 1 missed (3 or 5 sends), line 2 missed (7), line 3\nmissed (4 or 7), line 4 met (the only refusals, robotics funding ×3, justified), line 5 missed (right 7 or 5 of 13 against a scaled\n11; by written choices 6 or 4 against 9), line 6 not measured. Fault kinds: a stated plan left out of an event's reference (not\nshown to the judge; its effect untraced); a due day before the report that settles the event (the Rubin revenue question, upheld\nby both third readers; the CPO case split); \"and\" in the question against \"or\" in the Yes rung (MIIT, disputed among third\nreaders); parts left unlisted; a question leaning on an unnamed lab. The October and July readings used other articles and draws:\nthis does not isolate the effect of the library.\n\n**The due-date class, sized** (`due_day_census.py` → `due-day-census.txt`; a pattern screen, flagged cases read by hand): across\nevery stored written event answer, the only answers naming a periodic report as the sole settling material with the due day at\nthe period's end are six attempts of one matter (Rubin's FY2027 revenue, the same week-1 topic in two readings). Not a reason to\nopen a new version of the step.\n\n## Reading 1: week 2's openings (two families; `tally-openings.txt`)\n\n- **Re-opened a held question: 0 of 6** by both families. Same matter, another shape: capital spending for 2027 beside 2026 (both;\n  a year of its own, D38), the residual-value guarantee beside the credit-support total (one family; a signing question, D388).\n- Worth holding: 2 yes by both (capital spending 2027; the residual-value guarantee); 4 split yes/no (robotics funding, U.S.\n  gigawatts added in 2026, DRAM contract prices 2026, co-packaged-optics switch volumes).\n- Controls on 26 articles (the 6 openers and 20 drawn by seed): lost facts named by both families 0; wrong homes named by both 2\n  (an investment return under credit support; Micron's customer commitments under NVIDIA's supply commitments).\n- Lost questions both families name again and again: **the company's own numbers** (the quarter's revenue against the $108bn\n  guide, fiscal 2028 growth against 70%, margins, earnings) and **the $150bn buyback**. The first is the product rule (D382,\n  D384; D505: such figures should reach the judgements of related questions, not be questions of their own; not built).\n\n## Reading 2: every last answer (two families, planted and confirmed controls; `tally-answers.txt`)\n\n- **12 questions: supported by both 9; unsupported by both 0; split 3** (memory prices 2026: insufficient/supported; the credit\n  support total: the $108.5bn cap read as the amount, unsupported/supported; 2026 capital spending: $820bn by adding Amazon's\n  raise to the $800bn reference, unsupported/supported).\n- Controls: 4 planted wrong answers caught by both families (4 of 4; the plants are conspicuous contradictions between a choice\n  and its own reasons); 4 confirmed supported controls accepted by both (4 of 4; these are 4 of the 12 real answers, not\n  additional ones).\n- Statement fidelity, verified against the stored passages: `e590` says the Hugging Face CEO \"said he had just sold his company\"\n  and that the acquisition \"had been completed\"; the passage is TechCrunch's parenthetical, and completion is an inference (both\n  families flag it). `e279` labels Micron's November quarter \"fiscal Q1 2026\", copied from the article's title, not its passage\n  (one family). The first step's summary added what the passage does not hold.\n- The separate control reader (8 candidates) marked 3 not supported (U.S. gigawatts, memory prices, CPO volumes) and 1 unsure (the\n  residual-value guarantee). Across all three readers, **6 of 12 answers are uncontested** (supply commitments, China's Blackwell\n  approval, Rubin's revenue, the Hugging Face closing, MIIT's approval, 2027 capital spending) and 6 contested, for several\n  reasons: a cap read as the amount, a possible double count, qualitative evidence used to choose a numeric band, an event\n  forecast, and an answer-choice interpretation. Cases to trace one by one; not one proven mechanism.\n\n## Reading 3: did the answers get the facts that could change them? (a reader lead, not a test; `claude-sources.jsonl`, `codex-sources.jsonl`)\n\nFive questions drawn by seed (supply commitments, China's Blackwell approval, 2026 and 2027 capital spending, the residual-value\nguarantee), each read with its last request and up to six of the fortnight's articles on it. No family named an undelivered fact\nthat would move an answer; a few that would change its confidence. **The reading fell short of its frozen plan:** the packet\nshowed the request but not the last answer itself; it had no separate negative control; the readers listed absent facts\nthemselves instead of a code classification of every listed fact. The positive control (PRD 10's custom-chip group) was caught by\nthe Claude-family reader and missed by the Codex-family reader. A lead from one family on five questions, not a result.\n\n## Reading 4: did the company's own figures reach the questions they bear on? (D564; `figures_census.py`, `tally-figures.txt`)\n\nBy the statements' own fields (party NVIDIA, a typed financial figure): 270 kept statements in 61 groups of repeats. Against each of\nthe 12 judged questions' last request, the groups not shown and dated by its day: 46 to 61 a question. Two families apart read\nevery question with its whole last request and answer, the custom-chip question of July with its five facts mixed in as a positive\ncontrol and one statement already shown to the Rubin question as a negative.\n\n- **No pair that would move an answer, by either family.** Pairs named as changing only the confidence: NVIDIA's sales to the\n  largest cloud companies for the two capital-spending questions (both families on the 2027 one); revenue per gigawatt and\n  data-center revenue as a cross-check of U.S. gigawatts (Claude family only); cash-flow figures for the Hugging Face and\n  residual-value questions (Codex family only, the Claude family \"neither\").\n- **Controls.** Negative: neither family named the statement already shown. Positive: the Claude family named the two Broadcom\n  revenue figures as moving the answer (as they did, 9 of 9 sends, in PRD 10's test). The Codex family named nothing in the main\n  reading because the packet dated the control facts \"2026-07\" and left the negative's day empty: **my packet's fault**; on a\n  control packet with the real days it named four as confidence and the fifth \"cannot tell\", none as moving the answer. So a Codex-family \"no effect\" is weak evidence, as\n  in reading 3; the Claude family caught the control both times.\n- **What it shows:** among the selected figures and questions, neither family predicted an answer-choice change; the control and\n  selection limits leave a delivery gap unresolved. Limits (council round 12): the selector takes only statements whose party is\n  NVIDIA and whose typed measure matches a fixed list, not every financial fact; it drops a repeat group when any member was\n  shown, so a repeat's own details in an unshown member are not read (partly shown groups exist); readers saw summaries and\n  figures, not the source passages; a reader's \"would move\" is a prediction until a send tests it. Reading 1's largest missing\n  matter (the company's own figures) is first a matter of which questions exist (D382, D384: figures are evidence, not questions).\n- **Gate 1, per topic** (`faults_by_topic.py`, `faults-by-topic.txt`): the most frequent failing mark is a stated plan left out of an\n  event's reference (7 attempts, 3 topics), which is not shown to the judge; fixing it alone would make 2 more topics right\n  (9 or 7 of 13 against 11, a paper upper bound if that mark alone changed). No one kind of fault holds the gap.\n\n## Found on the way\n\n**Integration** (`INTEGRATION-CHECK.md`): the product's page server shows the new system's stored library as empty: the read side\nplaces questions in time by completed days, which the new system's writer never records. Gate 5's first concrete defect.\n\n## Limits\n\nOne draw; one company; one fortnight; week 2's later steps were regenerated with week 1's (not a live system's history); the\nreaders are two model families and one separate model reader; reading 3 is five questions. Nothing here compares the two systems\nor passes a gate.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,492p' AGENTS.md >/dev/null; sed -n '50,710p' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md >/dev/null; sed -n '/## 50\\\\./,/## 68\\\\./p' docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md >/dev/null; sed -n '/| D384 |/,/| D608 |/p' docs/DECISIONS.md >/dev/null\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
