{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md | tail -45'","aggregated_output":"its rung is reached by a fourth-quarter growth of about 25% that the judge itself calls an allowance; no shown piece gives the rate, and the\nshown 18% lands a rung lower. Called not supported by Codex alone: the clean path's credit-support total (a cap read as the amount);\nproduction's credit-support total and its first RTX Pro 5500 question (**both are confirmed supported controls**), the Hugging Face amount and\nthe Anthropic stake (both also called trivia in A). Cited statements with a field error: one in each system (a quarter mislabelled; \"more than\ndoubling to $115 billion\" written as \"will exceed\").\n\n## The rule, applied as written (LEAN-LOG §2)\n\n- First half (A): production covers two more of the matters both families listed. Met by production.\n- Second half (B): its share of judgements both families call supported is lower by 19 points, more than one in ten. Not met.\n- **Verdict: not clear. The next small step targets the largest difference observed, not a choice of system.**\n\nWhat weakens each half: A's three-matter gap is one sentence of the clean request, a product rule (D382), not a capability. B compares 7\njudgements with 15, so one judgement is 14 points for the clean path; the gap comes from one family, which parted from the separate reader on two of the four supported controls, both production items, with\nreasons that stand as a disagreement (a guarantee cap read as the amount; permission for two named firms read from \"some firms\"). As a\nsensitivity note only: with those two counted as the separate reader read them, production would stand at 12 of 15; the rule's count stays\n10 of 15. B at this size cannot say which system judges better.\n\n## The largest difference observed\n\nHow each system treats the company's own revenue and margin: three of the five matters, 145 kept statements no judgement reads on one side;\non the other, the same matters opened, with two or three duplicates among them and 126 statements piled on one question.\n\n## The source check the council asked for ($0, council round 11): do the articles hold a dispute, or only a number?\n\nClaude's first candidate for a next step was a narrow door on the clean path: open a revenue or margin question only when the item holds both\nthe company's own outlook and a stated market expectation for the same measure and period. Read against every article the readers listed\nfor M01–M03 and every article production opened its five such questions from:\n\n| matter | articles | hold such a pair | what they hold instead |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| M01 FY2027 revenue | 7 | **0** | the consensus alone ($406 billion, $412 billion, \"about 90% growth\"), or the company's guide for one quarter ($108 billion); the company gives no outlook for the year |\n| M02 FY2028 revenue | 8 | 2 with figures (70% guided \"against the 45% the Street had modelled\", a gap already closed: the consensus is now about $672 billion), 1 in words | the 70% outlook alone (5 articles) |\n| M03 FY2028 gross margin | 2 | 1 (the 72%–73% outlook, \"analysts assume margins hold roughly steady\", memory prices above what management expected) | the outlook alone |\n\n- **The pair does not cover the gap** (it never opens FY2027 revenue): the candidate is dropped, as its falsifier said.\n- **Why the readers listed these matters:** every one of their 24 revenue and margin entries gives the reason \"main driver\" (the company's\n  main number for the year), not a dispute. That is the standard's own question type, which D384 leaves out of the clean path and the\n  frozen question gold marks optional (may_open).\n- **A counter-example on production's side:** its data-center revenue question (v4) was opened from an article that holds only last\n  quarter's reported figure (\"$89 billion of data-center revenue out of $96.2 billion\"), no outlook and no expectation. It is the question\n  one family calls a duplicate of total revenue, and its judgement is the one both families call unsupported.\n- **So the choice is the plain one, and it is Alex's:** whether the new system holds questions on the company's main numbers at all\n  (D382, D384). The week shows what each answer costs; it does not show a narrower rule that would get both.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-5/own-reflection.md'","aggregated_output":"# My own reflection before the cold read (council-loop §10), 2026-11-16\n\n## What the record says stands between the clean system and adoption (`clean-arch/PRD.md` §8)\n\n| Gate | Result | What it measures |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1, the answer-choice step (D400, Alex's six lines) | not met in nine readings | the quality of the answer choices on questions already opened |\n| 2, the judge's test (D428) | not met; controls unexercised (4 of 8 comparable) | the judge on the new questions |\n| 3, end to end (D427, D431) | owed. Diagnostics: seeded 18, 18, 17 against 17, 15, 16 (inconclusive); same-day July census 2, 1, 0 against 1, 1, 1; **every loss at opening** (D395, D451) | whether the right questions reach a judged answer |\n| 4, use on unseen news (D484, proposed) | one week: **big matters covered 2 of 5 against 4 of 5**; last answers supported 6 of 7 against 10 of 15; \"not clear\" (D489) | what an analyst gets from a week |\n\n## What I think the last stretch got wrong\n\n- **Since D586 the loop has worked gate 1's residue:** line 5's reference, the postponement boundary, the fiscal note. Three $0 audits\n  closed with no candidate. Each was well run, but all three sit inside gate 1. Gate 1 measures the ladder on questions that were\n  opened.\n- **The largest demonstrated loss to an analyst on record is upstream:** big matters with no question (gate 4: 2 of 5 against the\n  old system's 4 of 5) and every end-to-end loss at opening (D451). D559 named the core problem \"forming answerable questions\". The\n  loop has not traced the gate-4 week's uncovered matters to where each was lost since D489.\n- **The live-store build was real progress for operation.** But adoption waits on quality, and quality's binding constraint looks like\n  coverage, not ladder polish.\n\n## The angle I would propose (for the cold reader to test, not to adopt)\n\n- A $0 trace of each big matter the new system missed in the gate-4 week (3 of 5) and in the same-day July census, from the\n  articles to where the matter was lost:\n  - Step 1 did not open it, because the rule \"only big matters open\" (D384) suppressed it, or because it was matched into an existing\n    broader question;\n  - opened in another shape;\n  - refused by the ladder;\n  - not judged.\n- **Falsifier:** if the losses scatter across stages with no shared mechanism, coverage has no bounded repair either, and the honest\n  state is that adoption waits on a design change only Alex can open.\n- **If one stage holds most of the losses**, that stage is the next work, measured against the old system on the same news.\n\n## My errors this stretch, for the cold reader to weigh\n\n- I stated that XR reaches no product reader, which was wrong for figures.\n- I changed my postponement lean without saying so.\n- I wrote several tests before reading the code they drive.\n- I reported a loose \"both sides\" count as evidence.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-library/RESULT.md | head -85'","aggregated_output":"# The small comparison of D559: the same 11 articles read from a kept library and from empty (D561), 2026-11-16\n\n**Answer: on these 11 selected articles, the read with last week's library re-opened none of the four questions it already\nheld and filed the identified facts under them; it opened 4 questions where the read from empty opened 16, none of them on a\nmatter the library held (both reader families). It opened three of the four missing matters the empty read opened (not the\nequity-investment commitments), so by the rule written before the run the result sits between \"supports going on\" and\n\"fails\", and is reported as it is. One draw; nothing about final answers.**\n\nRun: `poc/data/clean-carried-library-2026-11-16/` (22 of 22 reads complete, one call each, no resend; ledger $0.427 of $1.00).\nDesign and proofs: `DESIGN.md`, `proofs/`. My own read stored before the readers': `OWN-READ.md`. Readers (two families,\nblind to which read had the library in so far as the packet allows: the library shown is part of a read): `brief-readers.md`,\n`codex-readers.jsonl`, `claude-readers.jsonl`; tally `tally_readers.py` → `tally-readers.txt`.\n\n## The rule written before the run\n\n| Line | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Re-opens a held question in two or more of the four same-question cases | **0 of 4** (supply commitments, Hugging Face, Rubin's ramp, 2026 spending) |\n| Drops the matter's statements where the empty read kept them, in two or more | **0 of 4** by my own reading before the readers (`OWN-READ.md`): 1, 1, 2, 1 statements filed under the held question against 1, 1, 2, 1 kept by the empty read; the readers judged the homes, not a fact-by-fact comparison. Article 15's sentence holds both $800bn for 2026 and $1.3tn for 2027; it went under the 2026 question, and 2027 is tracked by neither read |\n| Opens two or fewer of the absent cases the empty read opens | opens **3 of the empty read's 4** (Groq's rack, the B200 price, Reflection AI; not the equity commitments), plus memory prices, which the empty read did not open |\n| Supports going on only if, besides the two lines above, the absent cases open as in the empty read | **not met** (3 of 4); not failed either: between the two, reported as it is |\n\n## What the readers say (both families unless split)\n\n| | Empty | Carried |\n|---|---|---|\n| Questions opened | 16 | 4 |\n| Of them, on a matter the library shown already held | 0 (no library) | **0** |\n| Worth holding | 12 yes; 3 yes/unsure; 1 yes/no (global AI spending as a share of U.S. GDP) | 1 yes; 3 yes/unsure (memory prices, Groq's rack, the B200 price) |\n| Statements filed under a held question | n/a | 27: right 17, wrong 2, unsure 2, split 6 |\n| Reader-listed entries of a matter deserving a question that the read neither opened nor held (both families' lists added per article and read; names not merged, so not distinct matters) | 25 | 18 |\n\n**The two homes both families call wrong:** customers' share of NVIDIA's receivables filed under the credit-support total\n(article 173); the CFO's 70% growth outlook filed under supply commitments (article 206; D508's readers had counted the same\nkind of statement as bearing on that question, so the line is disputed across readings).\n\n**What the carried read lost:** a question on a DOJ or FTC action against the Groq deal (opened from empty; the stored October\nrun did not open it either; one family names it missing for the carried read, the other did not mark its worth above\n\"unsure\"). The equity-investment commitments were not opened; their facts went under the held credit-support question, whose\nown outcome reads \"versus the equity investments it has made\", and both families call those four homes right: the held\nquestion's scope carries into the filing, and the separate equity-commitments question the empty read opened was not opened.\n\n**A gap the readers name in both conditions:** questions on the company's own numbers. The Claude-family reader names the\n$108bn quarterly outlook, the 70% growth outlook for fiscal 2028 and the gross-margin outlook cut to 72-73% on several\narticles; the Codex-family reader names gross margins and memory costs, 2028 growth, customer concentration and the funding\nof investments and payouts. These are missing questions, not missing facts: the figures were mostly kept, and in the carried\nread the $108bn outlook was filed under the China question. It is the standing product rule (D382, D384) and the item Alex\nruled on (D505: such figures should reach the judgements of related questions), not something this test changes.\n\n## Limits\n\nEverything above is one read of these articles from a fixed library, not behaviour over a changing library. One draw; 11 articles chosen because they opened topics (not a sample of the week); a seven-topic library one week old,\nitself opened from empty; the step's read of each article from a fixed library (no carry-over between articles); no\nmatching, answer choices or judging run. The empty reads differ from the stored October run of the same articles (12 and 35\nopened nothing; 15 opened a 2026-only question): run-to-run variation, one draw each.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'One next task|D608|D607|D606|spent|remaining|first-day|Idea planner' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | head -30\"","aggregated_output":"77:**Clean architecture Step 1 (2026-11-06, isolated work on `clean-arch`):** Alex reopened work with the clean architecture. An experimental prepared-source handoff now preserves the archived page, prior cleaned text, source-role decisions and selected-line mapping without changing the original database; quotations for prepared items must also occur contiguously in the original captured page. Two seven-item runs are available in the [clean architecture PRD](../clean-arch/PRD.md), one in the earlier selection order and one in recorded page-timestamp order. The source selector is not a production service and source ordering is not established event-arrival ordering. The runs expose unresolved semantic problems: citations can omit supporting facts despite an exact location match; model output can change a benchmark into a deployment, reverse a backup relation, omit a named customer or assign an unstated currency. A blinded 84-call check-placement/wording comparison and a 27-call same-article citation-completion diagnostic did not give a clean semantic fix and are not adopted. The latter missed an omitted connectivity condition and a reversed backup relationship, and left six expected evidence reviews unaddressed. A further five-round Codex–Claude council produced a narrowly scoped Step 1 link candidate, independently checked for prompt-contract drift. A six-article, 36-call blind comparison completed; the candidate still produced an explicitly self-contradictory link and both arms consistently omitted the same Kyber report and company response. It is not adopted and has not changed the active PRD prompt. A trace confirms that both the Kyber report and open Kyber thesis were supplied, and the raw model answers omitted the report and denial; the reason is not established. See ../poc/data/clean-step1-kyber-trace-2026-11-06/TRACE.md. An isolated six-call comparison showed that hiding the Kyber thesis did not recover the report or denial in any draw. A second six-call comparison returned them in 3/3 draws with the original Kyber paragraph alone and 0/3 with the full article; length, position and surrounding content changed together, so the reason is not isolated. Excerpt outputs have source-attribution limitations. Neither experiment changed state or established a production fix. (Superseded: the next task then was a whole-article coverage approach; the current next task is under \"One next task\".) See ../clean-arch/STEP1-IMPLEMENTATION-COUNCIL.md. The earlier four-round council agreed that no tested semantic fix is ready; its next investigation is a source-backed review of the 49-item historical run and its 160 evidence records, with overlapping issue flags and separate article-level omissions, then a separate comparison of the seven-item replays. See ../clean-arch/STEP1-COUNCIL-REVIEW.md. Preserve relevant evidence while identifying the next intervention; production/frozen history remains as described below. See [Step 1 run log](../clean-arch/STEP1-RUN-LOG.md) and [English reading page](../clean-arch/architecture.html).\n126:**Clean Step 1 source handoff council (2026-11-07):** The ongoing [council and offline checks](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-HANDOFF-COUNCIL.md) reconstructed 16 matching article-34 controls, all omitting a Kyber report and denial; the cause remains unknown. The 20-article saved source-role overlap review distinguished previously cited AI-generated summary lines and an unrelated recommendation from authored body. The clean runner does not send the saved source-role labels; the council chose to first compare original and previously selected source text on ten known articles. The isolated 60-call source-text comparison and condition-hidden review are complete; [results](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-TEXT-RESULTS.md) show specific contamination reductions alongside persistent omissions and changed meaning. It did not advance state or write production. The isolated six-article low-versus-medium source-fidelity diagnostic completed 36/36 calls and condition-hidden review. [Results](../clean-arch/STEP1-REASONING-FIDELITY-RESULTS.md) show partial improvements alongside persistent source-qualification and attribution concerns; no production setting is changed. The [prompt audit](../clean-arch/STEP1-FIDELITY-PROMPT-AUDIT.md) maps the observed failures to the full request and signed standard. The six-article isolated schema-description comparison completed 36/36 calls and condition-hidden review; the candidate did not preserve the repeated example qualification and is not adopted. [Results](../clean-arch/STEP1-SUMMARY-FIDELITY-RESULTS.md). A further six-article 36-call low-versus-medium comparison used corpus-cleaned sources outside the original 49-item clean replay and a fixed exploratory context; results were mixed, including unsupported links and incorrect attribution/date fields. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-ADDITIONAL-SOURCES-RESULTS.md). The structured-claims candidate was not sent after review revealed scope and complexity concerns. Council review of the next action is ongoing. The date-text schema-description diagnostic completed 48/48 calls on eight known cases, with mixed results; the candidate is not adopted. A selected-run census found twelve literal \"null\" strings in date-text fields, but no production writer impact is established. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-DATE-DESCRIPTION-RESULTS.md). A further preregistered eight-source date comparison completed 48/48 calls; the candidate lost a supported company-article statement date in all three draws on one source and is not adopted. [Results and replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-DATE-NEW-SOURCES-RESULTS.md). A bounded corpus census confirmed 163 source pages across three explicit generated-summary structures whose labels were removed while some summary text was retained; two NVIDIA cases were reproduced through the cleaner. [Source provenance investigation](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md). A read-only source-lineage replay reproduced 363/363 cleaned pages with current inputs, preserved ambiguous original-line locations, and surfaced the generated-summary label loss for review. [Source investigation and lineage replay](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-PROVENANCE-CENSUS.md). An offline neighboring-context observation exposed only 144 or 149 of 163 known labels and introduced many other page lines; it is not adopted as a general source fix. [Observations and viewer](../clean-arch/STEP1-SOURCE-CONTEXT-OBSERVATIONS.md). A new [saved-quote integrity investigation](../clean-arch/STEP1-QUOTE-INTEGRITY-CENSUS.md) reconstructed 360 saved answers across eight overlapping cohorts, including 78 prepared-source calls. Five saved unverified passage instances were complete matches under the existing normalization; an in-memory candidate recovered their original slices, while ten others remained unverified. The normalized source-slice lookup is now installed only in the isolated clean Step 1 runner; saved-answer and entry-point checks are recorded there. Page provenance, Unicode completeness, production resource budgets and writer integration remain open. The existing writer stores only one quote, whereas 63 of 160 evidence items in the 49-article exploratory trace have multiple passages. A [source-first 49-article coverage review](../clean-arch/STEP1-COVERAGE-CENSUS.md) separates material missing from the model input from source-visible omissions in the saved answers, with uncertain matter boundaries labeled. (Superseded: the next investigation then was why supplied material is missed; the current next task is under \"One next task\".) The canonical prompt and production configuration remain unchanged. Adding fallible role annotations remains a separate untested candidate. Council streams and handoffs are in `poc/data/clean-step1-ongoing-council-2026-11-07/`.\n159:## One next task\n310:**Where it stands (2026-11-16; D563 to D567; Alex not active, D439 in force; about $26.07 of D439's $40 spent):**\n350:- **The Idea planner (D580, D581):** a new-system three-choice event is shown to it as Yes and Still open. The design is parked as\n700:  numbers) was answered by him on 2026-11-15 (D505; see \"One next task\").\n702:  published rates); the current figure is in \"One next task\". (An earlier line here gave \"about $29.2\" as tracked spend; no decision or\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
