{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '159,245p' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\"","aggregated_output":"## One next task\n\n**Where the lean path stands (2026-11-15; D489 to D542).** Alex is not active (D509); D439 is in force: choices go to the\ncouncil (an independent Codex review and Claude) until consensus, recorded citing D439; nothing is pushed, deployed, published or\ncommitted; paid calls stay within D439's $40 ceiling (about $18.42 recorded; $0.0134 sent in this period, the ten judge calls of\nD511 and D519; the lean path $8.34 in all). Every stretch below is closed; its full record is in the decision log and in\n`research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md` (sections 1 to 43).\n\n- **The choice between the systems is not made.** The fresh week did not separate them (D489, \"not clear\"; nothing since ranks\n  them). The comparison that could choose by measurement was sized and not sent: at the proposed size it may miss differences\n  that matter ([sizing](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison/COMPARISON-SIZING.md), D517). **Production stays the default\n  and both systems stay (D518).** Alex's product choice on the company's financial figures stands (D505: evidence for related\n  questions, no table and no questions of their own; D382 and D384 stand).\n- **For Alex:** the [decision page](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/DECISION-PAGE-2026-11-15.md) (its section 7 is the one list\n  of what is his to choose, what he has decided and awaits building, and the defects with their evidence), the\n  [side-by-side week](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/side-by-side/SIDE-BY-SIDE-WEEK.md) and the\n  [judge note](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/unsupported/DESIGN-NOTE.md) with its one choice.\n\n**Open defects found on this path, each with its evidence; nothing is built on any of them:**\n1. **The new system's delivery gap** (D506, D508, D513, D514): a kept fact that bears on a question by a step of reasoning may be\n   linked to another question or to none, and so never reach that question's judge; the later-linking step skips a group whose\n   original statement arrived under another question. Three confirmed fact-and-question pairs in the fresh week, 23 unresolved\n   ([census](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/delivery-class/CLASS-CENSUS-RESULT.md)); one six-call test of its effect was\n   inconclusive ([result](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/effect/EFFECT-TEST-RESULT.md), D511). Paused.\n2. **The judge, shared by both systems** (D519, D520): on a question that asks for an amount it names a band when nothing shown\n   sizes the amount, or closes the last gap with a number of its own (36 of 438 stored readings, many of them the same\n   question read on successive days: a failure pattern on a few question paths, not an error rate;\n   [census](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/unsupported/UNSUPPORTED-CENSUS.md)). Three of the ten settled unsupported answers\n   coincided with a figure the system held and had not delivered to that question\n   ([result](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/missing-input/MISSING-INPUT-RESULT.md), D530 to D532). What the product shows is\n   Alex's choice (the judge note).\n3. **The old system's duplicate questions** (D520 to D523): three pairs in the fresh week; one second question was never compared\n   with the first, the others were compared and kept apart\n   ([result](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/duplicates/DUPLICATES-RESULT.md)).\n4. **The old system's filing under the broader question** (D529 to D531): the data-center revenue question never received the\n   next quarter's guidance or a consensus for the year, filed under total revenue only\n   ([cases](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/d375-measure/SAME-DAY-CASES-RESULT.md),\n   [trace](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/missing-input/FILING-TRACE-RESULT.md)). The relation `docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md` §2 names.\n5. **Where decisions and code part on dependencies** (D541, D542): `writing.write` drops an edge that would close a circle with a\n   note where PRD 06 says refuse and ask for a correction; PRD 06's \"historical only\" branch has a reader and no writer; the\n   label the seeding module writes on every seed edge (`last_end`) is defined nowhere; no decision says what happens to a later\n   proposal with another direction for a pair already read.\n\n**Decided by Alex, awaiting implementation and acceptance (not asked again):**\n- **D375, each article sees the questions committed before it.** A passed, bounded serial proof with labelled fake answers\n  ([result](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/duplicates/D375-PROOF-RESULT.md), D526, D528); the eligible same-day cases of the\n  fresh week read (D529). A real measurement needs a new version of the reading request and a paid run; not opened.\n- **D368 item 2, the matching step chooses a new question's dependencies.** In the unseeded fresh week one clear case among 97\n  pairs (data-center revenue reading total revenue;\n  [census](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/DEPENDENCY-SELECTION-CENSUS.md), D537). As the code stands\n  one stored edge has two readers (whose conclusion to read; which of two homes is the narrower): the same edge would remove\n  seven filing links ([proof](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/EDGE-PROOF-RESULT.md), D538). A design that\n  reads the two uses apart is recorded as **a provisional candidate, not sound for build**\n  ([design](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md), D539 to D542): two proofs on stored\n  data, the package's suite run under it, every stored dependency row classed. If the slice is reopened, its review must first\n  settle the cycle through an awaited question at creation, closing behaviour, a theme shown twice, the historical readers and\n  the label. A statement's home is not something an edge can decide (its section 2.5): the reading step's, the filing phase's\n  subject. No selection call is designed; nothing was sent.\n- **D368 item 4, the reading direction for preset questions** (settled by Claude on Alex's delegation): not measured (D536); the\n  stored seeded draws already agree with the frozen reference on 15, 15 and 16 of 17 questions; the rebuild and dry-run harness\n  is kept ([page](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-channel/CHANNEL-ASSESSMENT.md)).\n\n**The choice is made by the council under D439 (D544, 2026-11-15): the work toward production carries forward on the new\nsystem; the old system stays the running default until the new one passes its gates; both remain.** Nothing that runs is\nswitched, deleted or deployed. It is not a finding that the new system's answers are better: the cold reflection (D543) found\nnothing that ranks the two systems' answers, and the first consensus left the choice to Alex; that deferral was withdrawn the\nsame day, because his words in D439 give the council the job of taking a course. Reasons: he had reopened work on the rebuild\nand D439's scope names its steps; it follows the product rule on financial figures he last confirmed (D505); the fresh week\ngives no demonstrated reason to abandon it and shows fewer trivial or duplicate questions in that one run. Kept in view: its\nanswer-choice step has not met its lines, Stage B did not pass, integration is undone, and its cost and time to production are\nunknown. **Alex's word overrides this at any time**; it is also reconsidered on a change of his product rule, a sound comparison\non shared subjects that favours the old system, or the rebuild failing its unchanged gates within a bound agreed later. A first\ncheckpoint: $5 of further spending without a candidate that passes its prewritten small test returns the direction to the\ncouncil.\n\n**Since the choice (D545 to D550, all under D439):**\n\n- **The fresh week's answer choices, read and traced (D545 to D547).** Of 21 attempts on seven questions, one agreed fault of\n  Alex's lines (a condition of the topic left out of the choices, six attempts); ranges written with no figure were overrun by\n  the first filed amount on two questions (the old system shares this). A census of 49 amount questions and an audit of the\n  request found an undefined term (\"the topic's wording\") and no mechanism general enough to design for; no prompt change\n  ([result](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/fresh-ladders/FRESH-LADDERS-RESULT.md),\n  [audit](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/fresh-ladders/PROMPT-AUDIT-LINE-2.md)).\n- **The gates the new system must pass (D548), in order:** the answer-choice step on Alex's lines (D400), not passed; the\n  judge on the system's own questions (D428), not passed; the end-to-end comparison with Step 2's checks (D427, D431), still\n  owed, \"beats\" not yet defined in numbers; use on unseen news (D484), its lines proposed and not his; integration and\n  release, not written ([frame](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/NEW-SYSTEM-FRAME.md)).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"agent_message","text":"**The clean system is not ready to replace the running one.** The largest demonstrated loss is that important company financial information can be saved without reaching a question or an answer. Separately, the answer-choice step has not passed Alex’s gate, and the final-answer and end-to-end tests remain incomplete.\n\nOne concrete example: a stored article reported NVIDIA’s fiscal 2028 revenue-growth outlook of **70%**, against the **45%** analysts had previously expected. The clean system kept that statement, but opened no question and left it unlinked. Its own reasoning cited the instruction against opening a question on a financial measure. I checked the source passage, request, raw response and saved result at step 16 in the [stored run](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-lean-week-2026-11-14/week-r2/c1/step1/trace.sqlite>). That is a visible loss of a way to follow the outlook; it does **not** by itself prove that a particular existing answer would have changed.\n\n### 1. What stands between the system and adoption\n\nRanked by likely impact on an analyst:\n\n1. **Important matters can have no answer to follow.** In the fresh week, both reader families identified five major matters; the clean system covered two and the running system four. The three clean misses were revenue and margin matters excluded as questions by the product rule. The clean system also kept 145 statements about the company’s own figures that no judgement read. This is a real consequence of the current design in that empty-library run, although the two-family judgement that all three deserve questions is not Alex’s decision. Alex later confirmed that these figures should inform related questions, rather than become questions of their own; that delivery is not yet established. [Week result](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md), [D505](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS.md:849).\n\n2. **A question can exist but receive incomplete or unreliable support.** The record identifies three confirmed fact-and-question pairs where a relevant saved fact did not reach the question, plus 23 unresolved pairs. A test of the effect was inconclusive. The shared judge can also select an amount band without sufficient support: 36 of 438 stored readings show the pattern, often repeated days of the same question, so this is **not a 36/438 error rate**. In the two-week clean run, none of 12 last answers was rejected by both families, but six were contested by at least one reader; two statements over-read their sources. [Current-state defects](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/CURRENT_STATE.md:174), [fortnight result](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-run/RESULT.md).\n\n3. **Some answer choices misstate or omit what the question asks.** On the fresh five topics, the frozen step missed the lines about listing omitted parts and covering outcomes, and only **2 or 1 of 5** topics counted as right, depending on unresolved disagreements. The topic about custom silicon omitted a part; one Taiwan-controls answer treated a continuing proceeding as ruled out. These are product-visible issues. But much of the score also turns on reference marks that, in the traced cases, would not alter what the page or judge sees. [Fresh comparison](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/unlisted-parts/RESULT-FRESH-A2.md), [line-5 trace](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/unlisted-parts/fresh-a2/line5/RESULT.md), [postponement audit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/unlisted-parts/fresh-a2/postponement/AUDIT-RESULT.md).\n\n4. **Adoption is also blocked by evidence and integration gates.** Gate 1 has missed all nine readings. Gate 2 has only four comparable controls against eight required, and its strictest last-answer reading missed; gate 3 remains owed; gate 4’s acceptance lines are proposed rather than Alex-approved. The live-store work has been tested on copies, but live operation and the Idea planner still need acceptance. These are adoption blockers even where a particular analyst loss has not been demonstrated. [PRD §§1.5, 7–8](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/PRD.md:126), [decision page](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/DECISION-PAGE-2026-11-16.md).\n\n### 2. Conclusions that are weaker than they look\n\n- **“The clean system lost three major questions” is conditional on the starting state and the product rule.** The fresh week started empty. A continuing library can give facts a home, though the small carried-library comparison was mixed: it reopened none of four held questions, but did not open one matter the empty read opened. It was one draw on 11 selected articles, with no final answers. The newer provisional decision is to use a real earlier library for the next product test. [Carried-library result](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-library/RESULT.md), [D606](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS.md:950).\n\n- **“Every end-to-end loss was at opening” does not mean every loss was an analyst-visible error.** In the July comparison, some questions were reasonable but differently shaped from the frozen reference; some boundaries were unsettled. The earlier trace found seven certain standard breaches among 16 graded losses, with several distinct mechanisms. It supports opening as the first point of measured loss, not one common cause or proof that downstream reasoning is generally correct. [Opening trace](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/TRACE.md), [typed-unit audit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/AUDIT-RESULT.md).\n\n- **Repeatable gate readings are not necessarily correct readings.** The fortnight’s repeated reading reproduced every line verdict and the same seven omitted-part failures, using the same reader families and method. That is useful repeatability, not independent validation. The fresh reference and due-date disputes show why. [Repeated reading](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/gate1-stick/RESULT.md), [fiscal-note audit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/unlisted-parts/fresh-a2/fiscal-note/RESULT.md).\n\n- **The fresh-week comparison does not establish a winner.** Its prewritten result was “not clear”: coverage favoured production, while the apparent support-rate difference relied on small samples and reader disagreement, including two supported controls one family rejected. Nor does the clean system’s retention of more facts establish that those facts reach useful answers. [Week result](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md).\n\n### 3. The next breakthrough angle\n\nI do **not** see a bounded change on record ready to run as a fix. The best next angle is a **$0, source-to-answer trace of financial-figure delivery in a continuing library**: take the known important figures, identify each related question that actually exists, and follow the fact through its saved record, links and exact final judging request. Include facts filed under a different question, not just unlinked facts, and read the source passages.\n\n- **Falsifier:** if the apparently missing figures either do not bear on any existing question, already reach its judging request, or have different causes that no one intervention covers, this is not a supported common delivery candidate.\n- **What would move it:** a substantial, counted class of source-backed facts that should inform existing questions but disappear through the same identifiable step, plus a stored-data proof that a proposed change delivers them without pulling in unrelated facts.\n- **What closes it:** the falsifier above, or a proposed change that cannot deliver the decisive cases or that introduces comparable wrong links. Finding a missing fact alone does not prove an answer changes; that needs a separately justified test.\n- **Spend:** **$0 for the trace.** No paid send is supported yet. A later bounded test would need a reviewed design, controls and its own ceiling under D439; the user’s approximately $10 remaining is an upper constraint, not a target.\n\nThis respects D505’s choice to use figures as evidence for related questions. It also tests an actual delivery defect rather than reopening the rejected proposal to create financial questions. The fortnight’s figure census is a lead, but its fixed selector, partly shown groups and reader controls leave the delivery question open. [Fortnight result, reading 4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-run/RESULT.md), [main-numbers probe](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/main-numbers/RESULT.md).\n\n### 4. Can gate 1 be met by a bounded change on record?\n\n**No bounded change on record is shown to meet it as accounted.** A2 improved some marks but its fresh comparison had too few independent topics, a missed plant and reader disagreements; it was not accepted. On the fortnight, even the paper recount setting aside *both* omitted-part and reference marks reaches only **9 or 7 of 13**, against a scaled diagnostic target of 11. On the five fresh topics, setting aside reference marks alone reaches **3 or 2 of 5**. Neither recount changes Alex’s six lines or passes the gate. [A2 result](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/unlisted-parts/RESULT-FRESH-A2.md), [repeated reading](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/gate1-stick/RESULT.md), [fresh line-5 trace](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/unlisted-parts/fresh-a2/line5/RESULT.md).\n\nThat is not proof that the gate is impossible. It is also not proof that gate 1 is the largest **product** loss. The stronger product evidence points upstream: a good answer-choice step cannot answer a question that was never formed or a fact that never reached it. Conversely, improving opening or delivery alone would not satisfy the unchanged gate. Both constraints remain.\n\n### Comparison with Claude’s reflection\n\nI agree with Claude that the recent gate-1 audits did not produce a repair, that the live-store work is real progress, and that upstream coverage deserves attention. I also agree with tracing before spending.\n\nI differ on two points. First, the record already traces the fresh week’s three revenue/margin misses to the explicit opening rule, and the July opening losses were traced individually; repeating that trace alone is unlikely to reveal a new shared cause. Second, finding that most losses occur in one **stage** would not establish one repair: the July trace found multiple mechanisms within opening. I would therefore focus the next trace on the still-open D505 delivery question, while preserving the distinction between a missing question and an undelivered fact. [Claude’s reflection](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-5/own-reflection.md).\n\n**Recommended next steps, ranked:**\n\n1. **Trace financial-figure delivery through a carried library at $0.** Stop if the missing cases have no shared, fixable cause or do not bear on existing questions.\n2. **Only if that trace supports a candidate, prove it on stored data with wrong-link controls.** Stop if it fails to recover the decisive cases or adds comparable irrelevant links.\n3. **Keep gate 1 unresolved and unchanged.** Revisit a candidate only when evidence shows it can address the accounted failures without merely changing how they are read.\n\nThis is my independent review; I have not conducted a new council round or claimed consensus with Claude. No files were changed and no paid calls were made.\n\n"}}
{"type":"turn.completed","usage":{"input_tokens":857364,"cached_input_tokens":756736,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5595,"reasoning_output_tokens":144}}
